Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: cache SM7675 decoder CAPTURE MMAP buffers

Use the existing vb2 DMA-contiguous streaming allocation and cache-maintenance
path for native decoder MMAP output. Shared exported client surfaces retain
their own allocation policy. Imported DMA-BUFs, compressed input, encoders and
other platforms keep their existing behavior. No cache synchronization is
skipped.

The generic allocator choice follows the cacheable CAPTURE experiment in
CFM880/nabu-iris 6323e3184ec6156e44f1fe894cbcc221341cb38a, iris_vb2.c.
SM8150/HFI Gen1 and SM7675/HFI Gen2 are different platforms: no IOVA hole,
firmware packet, register, frequency or board value is ported. Uke uses
upstream vb2's existing DMA_FROM_DEVICE direction and paired prepare/finish.
The standalone queue-setup fixture covers import, encoder and legacy limits;
physical cache integrity and sustained Chrome throughput remain separate gates.

Link: https://github.com/CFM880/nabu-iris/blob/6323e3184ec6156e44f1fe894cbcc221341cb38a/kernel-overlay/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
@@ -117,6 +117,10 @@
 
 	core = inst->core;
 	f = V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(q->type) ? inst->fmt_src : inst->fmt_dst;
+	/* Use vb2's streaming DMA cache maintenance for CPU-readable output. */
+	if (core->iris_platform_data == &sm7675_data && inst->domain == DECODER &&
+	    V4L2_TYPE_IS_CAPTURE(q->type))
+		q->non_coherent_mem = q->memory == VB2_MEMORY_MMAP;
 
 	if (*num_planes) {
 		if (*num_planes != f->fmt.pix_mp.num_planes ||
